{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794174272,"nonce":"51Uo9Az57LLo47lcOX7QMdgwIOg=","message":"Landed on `roadmap-e90c710-integration` (fb33eb2..f6c9707).\n\n**Changes**\n- Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock: added rfd 0.18 (async folder picker)\n- src/app.rs: new. App state, Message, LoadState, per-repo entries. Stale-while-revalidate boot from snapshot, async discover then fingerprint then gitbug::list (one task per repo, 4-permit semaphore, epoch-guarded). Snapshot write-back per repo. 5s tick plus window-refocus tracking. Spinner subscription. Add/Remove/Rescan roots, persisted theme. 13 unit tests.\n- src/main.rs: App moved out; added Section::Repositories (default, first in nav); subscription wired.\n- src/ui/screen.rs: Repositories page (roots card, repo cards with status and open/closed counts, skeleton cards). Sidebar header and top-bar pills now show workspace data. Live sync pill (\"Scanning…\", \"Loading n/m…\", \"N failed\", \"Synced \u003cago\u003e\").\n- src/ui/components.rs: added `skeleton` and `spinner_dot`.\n- src/theme/style.rs: added neutral_dot, accent_dot, skeleton, banner styles.\n- src/mock.rs: removed the unused WORKSPACE and WORKSPACE_PATH constants.\n\n**Gates:** tests ok · clippy ok · fmt ok\n**Review:** 2 findings — 1 auto, 0 by hand, 1 deferred\n- Repos in `Error` state are not retried by the 5s tracker (only Ready and Locked are). Retrying would hit permanently broken or deleted repos every 5s. Recovery is by Rescan. To change it, add `LoadState::Error(_)` to the `matches!` in `check_tracked`.\n\n**Decisions**\n- `App::boot` reads workspace.json and the cache snapshot synchronously, before the window opens, so cached repos render on the first frame. `update` and `view` do no I/O.\n- Epoch counter drops results from superseded scans and tracking batches. Rescan during a refresh is safe; the cost is that dropped in-flight results are recomputed.\n- A corrupt workspace.json falls back to defaults, shows a banner, and disables saving so the file is never overwritten.\n- Tracking ticks stay hidden (no pill progress) until a repo actually needs a reload.\n- `GBTRACKER_THEME` still overrides the persisted theme at boot (dev convenience).\n- Not run: the manual acceptance items (window responsive with 10+ repos; folder picker persisting to workspace.json across restart). The GUI was not launched because it would write to the user's real config and cache dirs.\n- Saves are not sequenced; two rapid saves landing out of order is theoretically possible. Each write is atomic, so the file can't be corrupted.","files":null}]}